From 3c0a364d6a7579c49d319c2e39d51b40ef3b5cc3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tommy <tommy@pham.cc>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 03:37:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 74/75] Rollback: incremental RDRAM snapshots through a Windows
 write watch

RDRAM is allocated with MEM_WRITE_WATCH (PS2X_RDRAM_WRITE_WATCH=0: heap as before). Every capture/restore
collects the pages written since the last one (GetWriteWatch, reset) and stamps them with a sequence number;
a snapshot remembers the sequence it was filled at, so filling it again copies only the pages written since
(by the game or by a restore), and a restore copies back only those. Netplay pair at RTT 100: ~185 of 8192
pages per capture, capture 1.6 -> 0.4 ms, restore 1.6 -> 0.5 ms. PS2X_RB_INCREMENTAL=0: full copies;
PS2X_RB_WW_VERIFY=1 compares every copy with the whole memory (0 mismatching pages in a 6000-frame pair).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
